/* ============================================================
   F/A-18C HORNET · CONTROLS
   Coordinates are pixels in the 1920x1080 space of each view image.

   view    'front'   forward instrument panel, UFC, IFEI, AMPCD, standby
           'panels'  everything below the glare shield, in one frame:
                     left knee panel, centre pedestal, right knee panel,
                     both consoles and the canopy rails

   EVERY VIEW IS A SINGLE STRAIGHT CROP of the cockpit drawing. Nothing is
   moved, rotated or rearranged to fit the frame. Where a panel is too long to
   read in one view — the left console runs fore to aft — it is split into
   SEQUENTIAL views along its own axis, named for where it sits in the jet. If
   a switch is on the left console aft, it is on the aft tab, on the left.

   GENERATED, NOT TYPED. The hotspots were measured against the full cockpit
   layout drawing, and tools/compose.py cut that drawing into the four view
   images above while recording the transform for every piece it placed. Both
   the pixels and these rects went through that one transform, so the picture
   and the hitboxes cannot drift apart. Re-cut the views and regenerate; do not
   nudge numbers here by hand unless you are correcting a measurement.

   states  listed cold-jet-first, which is the position a parked Hornet is
           found in, so `init` is always states[0].
   ============================================================ */

